xt_representativeness":0.9072901010513306,"text_excerpt":"I already miss Blue Plate Cafe even though they just closed about a month and a half ago. I liked the funny name and the whimsical decor. On the restrooms instead of signs that said \"men\" or \"women\" they had a Barbie doll on the ladies room and a Ken doll on the men's room. How cute is that?! The food was great and portions were huge and service was stellar. I read that the owner just got burnt out and closed down the restaurant for some much needed rest and relaxation. I hope that she's getting lots of that and am keeping my fingers crossed that she decides to open another great breakfast place in Nola one of these days. Rest in piece Blue Plate Cafe. You will be dearly missed."},{"business_id":"LK58peZTR54sYsISrTo0cA","review_id":"nX8a_vmVrAmF7uBeNkDmmQ","date":"2013-08-18T17:48:57","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9013698101043701,"text_excerpt":"This place is so awesome we went for breakfast one day and lunch the next. Erin is super nice and attentive. We had great service and even met the owner who is also the chef. Everything on the menu sounds delicious so it was hard to settle on 1 item so my boyfriend and I shared a couple plates.. we were so pleased with everything about this cute little restaurant.. You will NOT be disappointed."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
